option {:value "2008531"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008542"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008559"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008572"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008594"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008609"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008621"} "Canadian Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008638"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255468"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255607"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255701"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255809"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255953"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256092"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256226"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256337"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258763"} "2008"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/162"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2180"} "National Olympic Nautical Stadium d'Île-de-France, Vaires-sur-Marne, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2008517"} "40 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Men’s K2-500 returned to the canoe sprint Olympic Programme for the first time since 2008, although the event was on the Olympic Programme continuously from 1976-2008."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The event was considered wide open as the last five World Championships had seen five different nations take home gold medals. In 2023, the Portugal pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/135552"} "João Ribeiro"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/146031"} "Messias Baptista"] " had taken World gold. Germany had the world #1 ranked double in Martin Hiller and Tamas Gesco, but they would not compete at Paris, as the Germans sent out " [:a {:href "/athletes/143394"} "Jacob Schopf"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/143395"} "Max Lemke"] ". Schopf had won silver in the K2-1000 at Tokyo 2020, alongside " [:a {:href "/athletes/116560"} "Max Hoff"] ", while Lemke had taken gold in 2020 in the K4 event."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Schopf and Lemke would come through for the gold medal. After winning their heat and semi-final, however, they were challenged in a close final by the Hungarian duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/143673"} "Bence Nádas"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/136538"} "Sándor Tótka"] ", coming from behind to win gold by only 0.28 seconds. The German’s winning time of 1:26.87 was a new Olympic best for the event. Taking bronze was the Australian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/140744"} "Jean van der Westhuyzen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/140745"} "Tom Green"] ", who had won gold in K2 at Tokyo 2020, but over 1,000 metres."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Nádas had been the 2022 World Champion in this event, paddling with " [:a {:href "/athletes/134360"} "Bálint Kopasz"] ". Kopasz competed at Tokyo 2024 and in this event, but he was partnered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/143671"} "Ádám Varga"] ", and they made only the consolation final. Kopasz and Varga would seem a formidable pair, taking silver and bronze in Paris in kayak singles, but they finished only 15th overall in K2-500."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "122/119"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143394"} "Jacob Schopf"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/143395"} "Max Lemke"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "1:28.03 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:28.13 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:26.87 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "141/142"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143673"} "Bence Nádas"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/136538"} "Sándor Tótka"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1:29.08 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:28.38 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:27.15 (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15/13"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140744"} "Jean van der Westhuyzen"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/140745"} "Tom Green"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:28.59 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:26.85 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:27.29 (3 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "95/91"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/151222"} "Adrián del Río"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/133655"} "Marcus Cooper"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {} "1:35.26 (3 h1)"] [:td {} "1:29.12 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:27.